  "summary": "The third round's proposal is nearly implementation-ready but overlooks two practical issues. First, it says to place the ideation_prompt injection 'after the description but before the task section' in ideating.md, but the current template already has a {previous_ideation} placeholder between the description and the --- separator that precedes the task section — the proposal doesn't clarify how the new {ideation_prompt_section} relates to {previous_ideation}, and inserting both could create a cluttered preamble where the LLM has to parse existing ideation, user direction, AND the task/role instructions in sequence. The cleaner approach is to fold the user direction into the {previous_ideation} block or place it immediately after the --- separator but before the ## Task heading, making it visually and semantically distinct from the feature description context above the separator. Second, all three rounds assume the edit modal is the right primary entry point for setting ideation_prompt, but the user's description specifically mentions 'when moving to ideation as a modal' — this means the 'Move to Ideating' action (both in TUI and WebUI) should prompt for the seed text at transition time, not just rely on the user remembering to pre-edit the field. The implementation should add an optional text input to the move-to-ideating confirmation flow so the field gets set atomically with the phase transition, reducing the chance of stale or forgotten seeds."
}
